 "structural_change": "DRIVE-S81-LEPNH r5b (10-20), successor of r4m (full core rows, no region; GRT overflow 0, native32 PASS). CLOCK (r4m gate 18:28 FAIL TT/FF pin-flop spread 114.6/106.8): clock_split_km K=8 made 8 local BUFx24 roots over clusters of 658..2,879 sinks spanning up to 325 um; TritonCTS builds each cluster net alone (path depth 4..6) and the 8-sink top H-tree (570 um avg sink wire) does not see the subtree latency, so cluster roots arrive unequal. The pre-native kit s81sl_lepnh (one TritonCTS tree, no KM) measured 40.2/36.8. r5 drops the KM split: ONE balanced TritonCTS tree over the whole tile. r5b: explicit sink clustering 24 sinks / 30 um, 15-um buffer spacing, -balance_levels (the dsfd_vm_direct_scatter cb3 recipe: spread 63 -> 28 ps). RX (r4m path_classes: 297 macro->reg paths, worst -94.9 ps TT at placement: RX SRAM q (32x128 rows across the full width) -> rid -> E-face ri pin over up to ~430 um in one cycle, the RX twin of the S81-FIX3 TXRP route failure): RTL RXOP=1 adds an RX output stage -- rid/riv stay beside the RX SRAM rows, ri leaves a second flop rank at the E face (+1104 flops, +1 lane->ri edge on the elastic off-die receive path; beat order/content unchanged; phase miter vs slice3 reference with ri delayed 1 PASS; mutant RXOPSKEW FAIL). Same outline 475.2x561.6, macros, pins, SDC as r4m.",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Source-registered as s81sl_lep / s81sl_lepnh (ro / li / ml_rd land in pin flops, ri / lo / ml_wd / mu_rt / fault leave flops); recipe pin_regs would add an unpriced stage."
 },
